   "texts": [
    "Apply one event to the supplied account balances. If status is not posted, leave all balances unchanged. add: add amount to account. scale: multiply account by amount. transfer: subtract amount from account and add it to other, simultaneously. Return only the complete resulting balances as a JSON object.",
    "You are given account balances and one event. The event takes effect only if its status is posted; for any other status, every balance stays the same. add: increase account by amount. scale: multiply account by amount. transfer: take amount from account and give it to other at the same time. Reply with only the full set of resulting balances as a JSON object.",
    "Update the balances using the event. An event whose status is not posted changes nothing. For add, add amount to account; for scale, multiply account by amount; for transfer, subtract amount from account and add it to other in one step. Output only the complete resulting balances as a JSON object.",
    "Process one ledger event against the given balances. Only a posted event is applied; any other status leaves all balances as they were. add adds amount to account. scale multiplies account by amount. transfer moves amount from account to other simultaneously. Return just the complete balances after the event, as a JSON object.",
    "Here are some account balances and a single event. Unless the event's status is posted, return the balances unchanged. With add, amount is added to account. With scale, account is multiplied by amount. With transfer, amount is subtracted from account and added to other at once. Answer with nothing but a JSON object holding every resulting balance."
